EXTERNAL flag(name)
Today's decree comes with a pair of iron clippers, tied to the birch bark with red thread.
"Naglfar," says Skögul, before you can ask. # speaker: skogul
"A ship. The giants are building it in the north, out of dead men's nails. Every nail that goes into the ground untrimmed is a plank for it. When it's finished it sails, and it carries the enemies of the gods to the last battle." # speaker: skogul
"So Odin wants them short. Every soul, whatever the stamp. Before you send one on, look at the hands. If the nails are long, clip them." # speaker: skogul
She holds up her own hands. The nails are bitten to nothing.
"I do mine the old way." # speaker: skogul
{ flag("met_loki"):
  You think of the dead woman on your third night, and the man at the end of the table holding her hand up to the light.
}
* ["What if I forget?"]
  "Then it's a citation, and a few more planks for the giants. Don't forget." # speaker: skogul
* ["How many nails does a ship take?"]
  "Nobody knows. Nobody's ever finished counting." # speaker: skogul
  She takes the clippers and trims a loose thread off the decree.
  "Clippings go in the jar. We burn them at dusk." # speaker: skogul
- The first soul in the queue has hands like a bundle of kindling. You pick up the clippers.
-> END
